{"id": "EUVD-2026-80634", "enisaUuid": "bf8aacf0-2307-368c-b919-3a67b962db00", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: typec: qcom-pmic: cancel reset_work on stop\n\npdphy_stop() disables IRQs but leaves reset_work pending.  If the IRQ\nhandler schedules it just before disable_irq(), the work runs after\nremove() frees the struct via devm.\n\nCall cancel_work_sync() after disabling IRQs to close the window.\n\nThis issue was found by an in-house static analysis tool.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:33:29", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:56:42", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0b69b166852dbf1f9532b22bd49f502e5970eb95", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b9a7eed472edbfa8dec0fdeafd5e796550a8a8b7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d4e00a1eb39174e25ef759b8fb1111bba8e87b1e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/52d556f08547733948cc40b8b11e6b68dccee7b2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7b0df6efd143f8085bdb68778a013a46f1349913"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90026", "GHSA-7634-6gf7-r2f6"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1abfc2e6-9dee-3ee9-b9f1-72445e4a3c54", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a4422ff221429c600c3dc5d0394fb3738b89d040 <0b69b166852dbf1f9532b22bd49f502e5970eb95"}, {"id": "2d577365-4112-3ff9-8a75-62e2dc36d562", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}, {"id": "38a9c1fd-2a15-3096-865e-5f6c80b76ef4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "534fcdd6-7845-329f-9082-4573e127f34f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a4422ff221429c600c3dc5d0394fb3738b89d040 <52d556f08547733948cc40b8b11e6b68dccee7b2"}, {"id": "53890649-d322-3ab5-9789-755c5b71d31b", "product": {"name": "Li